manufacture-zero-state: zero all TPM state at manufacture

Classification: platform setting.

TPM_Manufacture() initializes only some fields of the persistent, orderly,
state-reset and state-clear data. All of them (and the persistent NV area)
are zeroed first so that the fields not written explicitly (e.g. resetCount,
timeEpoch, algorithmSet) start at 0, as in a freshly manufactured tpm-rs,
rather than at 0xff or values left from an earlier instance.

diff --git a/src/Manufacture.c b/src/Manufacture.c
--- a/src/Manufacture.c
+++ b/src/Manufacture.c
@@ -114,6 +114,16 @@ TPM_Manufacture(
     // initialize NV
     NvManufacture();
 
+    // tpm-rs differential testing: zero all RAM state structures and the
+    // persistent NV area so that fields not explicitly written below (e.g.
+    // resetCount, timeEpoch, algorithmSet) start at 0 rather than 0xff or stale
+    // values from a previous trace.
+    MemorySet(&gp, 0, sizeof(gp));
+    NvWrite(NV_PERSISTENT_DATA, sizeof(gp), &gp);
+    MemorySet(&go, 0, sizeof(go));
+    MemorySet(&gr, 0, sizeof(gr));
+    MemorySet(&gc, 0, sizeof(gc));
+
     // Clear the magic value in the DRBG state
     go.drbgState.magic = 0;
 
